t":"わかりやすかった","ts":"1624881232.177500","team":"T03C4RC8V","replace_original":false,"delete_original":false,"blocks":[{"type":"rich_text","block_id":"+f5Ip"}]},{"client_msg_id":"5F44D57B-331B-4EAF-B53F-16B419A8131A","type":"message","user":"UDDCM376D","text":"\u003chttps://qiita.com/UTDoi/items/d49ea919818d9b519f93|https://qiita.com/UTDoi/items/d49ea919818d9b519f93\u003e","ts":"1624881220.177000","attachments":[{"fallback":"Qiita: JavaScriptの非同期処理をできる限り正確に理解する - Qiita","id":1,"title":"JavaScriptの非同期処理をできる限り正確に理解する - Qiita","title_link":"https://qiita.com/UTDoi/items/d49ea919818d9b519f93","text":"プログラミング初心者が詰まりやすいポイントとして、非同期処理はよくあげられるかと思います。実際初心者にとっては概念自体もわかりにくいし、なぜか記事によって言い回しやら説明の仕方やらが違うので調べれば調べるほど混乱してきて、心が折れそう...","image_url":"https://qiita-user-contents.imgix.net/https%3A%2F%2Fcdn.qiita.com%2Fassets%2Fpublic%2Farticle-ogp-background-1150d8b18a7c15795b701a55ae908f94.png?ixlib=rb-4.0.0\u0026w=1200\u0026mark=https%3A%2F%2Fqiita-user-contents.imgix.net%2F~text%3Fixlib%3Drb-4.0.0%26w%3D840%26h%3D380%26txt%3DJavaScript%25E3%2581%25AE%25E9%259D%259E%25E5%2590%258C%25E6%259C%259F%25E5%2587%25A6%25E7%2590%2586%25E3%2582%2592%25E3%2581%25A7%25E3%2581%258D%25E3%2582%258B%25E9%2599%2590%25E3%2582%258A%25E6%25AD%25A3%25E7%25A2%25BA%25E3%2581%25AB%25E7%2590%2586%25E8%25A7%25A3%25E3%2581%2599%25E3%2582%258B%26txt-color%3D%2523333%26txt-font%3DHiragino%2520Sans%2520W6%26txt-size%3D54%26txt-clip%3Dellipsis%26txt-align%3Dcenter%252Cmiddle%26s%3Dab400b4c30e072d4d4878588ef3da730\u0026mark-align=center%2Cmiddle\u0026blend=https%3A%2F%2Fqiita-user-contents.imgix.net%2F~text%3Fixlib%3Drb-4.0.0%26w%3D840%26h%3D500%26txt%3D%2540UTDoi%26txt-color%3D%2523333%26txt-font%3DHiragino%2520Sans%2520W6%26txt-size%3D45%26txt-align%3Dright%252Cbottom%26s%3Df58cedb73ee3bae698561df6336907ab\u0026blend-align=center%2Cmiddle\u0026blend-mode=normal\u0026s=c3eedddeba1b02dd73b5efc27f879d73","blocks":null,"service_name":"Qiita","service_icon":"https://cdn.qiita.com/assets/favicons/public/apple-touch-icon-ec5ba42a24ae923f16825592efdc356f.png","from_url":"https://qiita.com/UTDoi/items/d49ea919818d9b519f93","original_url":"https://qiita.com/UTDoi/items/d49ea919818d9b519f93"}],"team":"T03C4RC8V","replace_original":false,"delete_original":false,"blocks":[{"type":"rich_text","block_id":"alIYK"}]},{"client_msg_id":"e7ff1be2-3f5b-4746-9129-63151112cec2","type":"message","user":"U022XK5866Q","text":"まさにそんな感じで、MDNには最初に返ってきた画像を表示という例がありますね。\n\u003chttps://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/Promise/any#displaying_the_first_image_loaded\u003e","ts":"1624841458.176100","attachments":[{"fallback":"Promise.any() - JavaScript | MDN","id":1,"title":"Promise.any() - JavaScript | MDN","title_link":"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/Promise/any#displaying_the_first_image_loaded","text":"Promise.any() takes an iterable of Promise objects and, as soon as one of the promises in the iterable fulfills, returns a single promise that resolves with the value from that promise. If no promises in the iterable fulfill (if all of the given promises are rejected), then the returned promise is rejected with an AggregateError, a new subclass of Error that groups together individual errors. Essentially, this method is the opposite of Promise.all().","image_url":"https://developer.mozilla.org/mdn-social-share.0ca9dbda.png","blocks":null,"service_name":"developer.mozilla.org","service_icon":"https://developer.mozilla.org/apple-touch-icon.0ea0fa02.png","from_url":"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/Promise/any#displaying_the_first_image_loaded","original_url":"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/Promise/any#displaying_the_first_image_loaded"}],"team":"T03C4RC8V","reactions":[{"name":"rikai","count":1,"users":["UDDCM376D"]}],"replace_original":false,"delete_original":false,"blocks":[{"type":"rich_text","block_id":"ReP"}]},{"client_msg_i